<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narasimha III (Hoysala)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1263–1292</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narasimha III was king of the Hoysala dynasty who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwarasamudra">Dwarasamudra</a>, while his half-brother Ramanatha held the Tamil territories. The division led to rivalry and war between the brothers. His general Somanatha built the Chennakeshava temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somanathapura">Somanathapura</a>. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veera-ballala-iii">Veera Ballala III</a>, who reunited the kingdom.</p></div>
